{
  "title": "36: Yaseen يس",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nيٰسٓ ۚ‏(1)\nYAASEEN.\nYa Seen!\nوَالْقُرْاٰنِ الْحَكِيْمِ ۙ‏(2)\nWAL QURAANIL HAKEEM.\nBy the Wise Quran,\nاِنَّكَ لَمِنَ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَۙ‏(3)\nINNAKA LAMENAL MURSALEEN.\nyou are indeed one of the apostles,\nعَلٰى صِرَاطٍ مُّسْتَقِيْمٍؕ‏(4)\nA’LAA SERAATIM MUSTAQEEM.\non a straight path.\nتَنْزِيْلَ الْعَزِيْزِ الرَّحِيْمِ ۙ‏(5)\nTANZEELAL A’ZEEZIR RAHEEM.\n[It is a scripture] sent down gradually from the All-mighty, the All-merciful\nلِتُنْذِرَ قَوْمًا مَّاۤ اُنْذِرَ اٰبَآؤُهُمْ فَهُمْ غٰفِلُوْنَ‏(6)\nLE-TUNZERA QAWMAM MAA UNZERA AABAA-OHUM FAHUM GHAAFELUN.\nthat you may warn a people whose fathers were not warned, so they are oblivious.\nلَقَدْ حَقَّ الْقَوْلُ عَلٰٓى اَكْثَرِهِمْ فَهُمْ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(7)\nLAQAD HAQQAL QAWLO A’LAA AKSAREHIM FAHUM LAA YOAMENOON.\nThe word has certainly become due against most of them, so they will not have faith.\nاِنَّا جَعَلْنَا فِىْۤ اَعْنَاقِهِمْ اَغْلٰلًا فَهِىَ اِلَى الْاَ ذْقَانِ فَهُمْ مُّقْمَحُوْنَ‏(8)\nINNAA JA-A’LNAA FEE A-A’NAAQEHIM AGHLAALAN FAHEYA ELAL AZQAANE FAHUM MUQMAHOON.\nIndeed We have put iron collars around their necks, which are up to the chins, so their heads are upturned.\nوَجَعَلْنَا مِنْۢ بَيْنِ اَيْدِيْهِمْ سَدًّا وَّمِنْ خَلْفِهِمْ سَدًّا فَاَغْشَيْنٰهُمْ فَهُمْ لَا يُبْصِرُوْنَ‏(9)\nWA JA-A’LNAA MIM BAYNE AYDEEHIM SADDANW WA MIN KHALFEHIM SADDAN FA-AGHSHAYNAAHUM FAHUM LAA YUBSEROON.\nAnd We have put a barrier before them and a barrier behind them, then We have blind-folded them, so they do not see.\nوَسَوَآءٌ عَلَيْهِمْ ءَاَنْذَرْتَهُمْ اَمْ لَمْ تُنْذِرْهُمْ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(10)\nWA SAWAAA-UN A’LAYHIM A-ANZARTAHUM AM LAM TUNZIRHUM LAA YOAMENUN.\nIt is the same to them whether you warn them or do not warn them, they will not have faith.\nاِنَّمَا تُنْذِرُ مَنِ اتَّبَعَ الذِّكْرَ وَخَشِىَ الرَّحْمٰنَ بِالْغَيْبِۚ فَبَشِّرْهُ بِمَغْفِرَةٍ وَّاَجْرٍ كَرِيْمٍ‏(11)\nINNAMAA TUNZERO MANIT-TABA-A’Z ZIKRA WA KHASEYAR RAHMAANA BIL-GHAYBE FA-BASH-SHIRHO BE MAGHFERATINW WA AJRIN KAREEM.\nYou can only warn someone who follows the Reminder and fears the All-beneficent in secret; so give him the good news of forgiveness and a noble reward.\nاِنَّا نَحْنُ نُحْىِ الْمَوْتٰى وَنَكْتُبُ مَا قَدَّمُوْا وَاٰثَارَهُمْؕؔ وَكُلَّ شَىْءٍ اَحْصَيْنٰهُ فِىْۤ اِمَامٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‏(12)\nINNAA NAHNO NOHYIL MAWTAA WA NAKTOBO MAA QADDAMOO WA AASAARAHUM, WA KULLA SHAY-IN AHSAYNAAHO FEE EMAAMIM MOBEEN.\nIndeed it is We who revive the dead and write what they have sent ahead and their effects [which they left behind], and We have figured everything in a manifest Imam.\nوَاضْرِبْ لَهُمْ مَّثَلًا اَصْحٰبَ الْقَرْيَةِ ۘ اِذْ جَآءَهَا الْمُرْسَلُوْنَۚ‏(13)\nWAZ RIB LAHUM MASALAN ASHAABAL QARYATE, IZ-JAA-A-HAL MURSALOON.\nCite for them the example of the inhabitants of the town when the apostles came to it.\nاِذْ اَرْسَلْنَاۤ اِلَيْهِمُ اثْنَيْنِ فَكَذَّبُوْهُمَا فَعَزَّزْنَا بِثَالِثٍ فَقَالُوْۤا اِنَّاۤ اِلَيْكُمْ مُّرْسَلُوْنَ‏(14)\nIZ ARSALNAA ELAYHEMUS NAYNE FA-KAZZABOOHOMAA FA-A’ZZAZNAA BE SAALESIN FA-QAALOO INNAA ELAYKUM MURSALOONA.\nWhen We sent to them two [apostles], they impugned both of them. Then We reinforced them with a third, and they said, ‘We have indeed been sent to you.’\nقَالُوْا مَاۤ اَنْتُمْ اِلَّا بَشَرٌ مِّثْلُنَا ۙ وَمَاۤ اَنْزَلَ الرَّحْمٰنُ مِنْ شَىْءٍۙ اِنْ اَنْتُمْ اِلَّا تَكْذِبُوْنَ‏(15)\nQAALOO MAA ANTUM ILLAA BASHARUM MISLONAA, WA MAA ANZALAR RAHMAANO MIN SHAY-IN IN ANTUM ILLAA TAKZEBOON.\nThey said, ‘You are no other than human beings like us, and the All-beneficent has not sent down anything, and you are only lying.’\nقَالُوْا رَبُّنَا يَعْلَمُ اِنَّاۤ اِلَيْكُمْ لَمُرْسَلُوْنَ‏(16)\nQAALOO RABBONAA YA’LAMO INNA ELAYKUM LA-MURSALOON.\nThey said, ‘Our Lord knows that we have indeed been sent to you,\nوَمَا عَلَيْنَاۤ اِلَّا الْبَلٰغُ الْمُبِيْنُ‏(17)\nWA MAA A’LAYNAA ILLAL BALAAGHUL MOBEEN.\nand our duty is only to communicate in clear terms.’\nقَالُوْۤا اِنَّا تَطَيَّرْنَا بِكُمْۚ لَئِنْ لَّمْ تَنْتَهُوْا لَنَرْجُمَنَّكُمْ وَلَيَمَسَّنَّكُمْ مِّنَّا عَذَابٌ اَلِيْمٌ‏(18)\nQAALOO INNAA TATAYYARNAA BEKUM, LA-IL-LAM TANTAHOO LA-NAR- JOMANNAKUM WA LAYAMASSANNAKUM MINNAA A’ZAABUN ALEEM.\nThey said, ‘Indeed we take you for a bad omen. If you do not desist we will stone you, and surely a painful punishment will visit you from us.’\nقَالُوْا طٰۤئِرُكُمْ مَّعَكُمْؕ اَئِنْ ذُكِّرْتُمْ ؕ بَلْ اَنْتُمْ قَوْمٌ مُّسْرِفُوْنَ‏(19)\nQAALOO TAAA-EROKUM MA-A’KUM, A-IN ZUKKIRTUM, BAL ANTUM QAWMUM MUSREFOON.\nThey said, ‘Your bad omens attend you. What! If you are admonished.... Indeed, you are an unrestrained lot.’\nوَجَآءَ مِنْ اَقْصَا الْمَدِيْنَةِ رَجُلٌ يَّسْعٰى قَالَ يٰقَوْمِ اتَّبِعُوا الْمُرْسَلِيْنَۙ‏(20)\nWA JAA-A MIN AQSAL MADEENATE RAJOLUN-Y YAS-A’A QAALA YAA-QAWMIT TABE-U’L MURSALEENAT.\nThere came a man hurrying from the city outskirts. He said, ‘O my people! Follow the apostles!\nاتَّبِعُوْا مَنْ لَّا يَسْئَلُكُمْ اَجْرًا وَّهُمْ مُّهْتَدُوْنَ‏(21)\nTABEOO’ MAL LAA YAS-ALOKUM AJRANW WA HUM MOHTADOON.\nFollow them who do not ask you any reward and they are rightly guided.\nوَمَا لِىَ لَاۤ اَعْبُدُ الَّذِىْ فَطَرَنِىْ وَاِلَيْهِ تُرْجَعُوْنَ‏(22)\nWA MAA LEYA LAA A-A’BODUL LAZEE FATARANEE WA ELAYHE TURJA-O’ON.\nWhy should I not worship Him who has originated me, and to whom you shall be brought back?\nءَاَ تَّخِذُ مِنْ دُوْنِهٖۤ اٰلِهَةً اِنْ يُّرِدْنِ الرَّحْمٰنُ بِضُرٍّ لَّا تُغْنِ عَنِّىْ شَفَاعَتُهُمْ شَيْئًا وَّلَا يُنْقِذُوْنِۚ‏(23)\nA-AT-TAKHEZO MIN DOONEHI AALEHATAN INY-YORIDNIR RAHMAANO BE-ZURRIL LAA TUGHNE A’NNEE SHAFAA-A’TOHUM SHAY-ANW WA LAA YUNQEZOON.\nShall I take gods besides Him? If the All-beneficent desired to cause me any distress, their intercession will not avail me in any way, nor will they rescue me.\nاِنِّىْۤ اِذًا لَّفِىْ ضَلٰلٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‏(24)\nINNEE EZAL LAFEE ZALAALIM MOBEEN.\nIndeed, then I would be in manifest error.\nاِنِّىْۤ اٰمَنْتُ بِرَبِّكُمْ فَاسْمَعُوْنِؕ‏(25)\nINNEE AAMANTO BE-RABBEKUM FAS-MA-O’ON.\nIndeed I have faith in your Lord, so listen to me.’\nقِيْلَ ادْخُلِ الْجَنَّةَؕ قَالَ يٰلَيْتَ قَوْمِىْ يَعْلَمُوْنَۙ‏(26)\nQEELAD-KHOLIL JANNAH, QAALA YAA LAYTA QAWMEE YA’LAMOONA.\nHe was told, ‘Enter paradise!’ He said, ‘Alas! Had my people only known\nبِمَا غَفَرَلِىْ رَبِّىْ وَجَعَلَنِىْ مِنَ الْمُكْرَمِيْنَ‏(27)\nBEMAA GHAFARA-LEE RABBEE WA JA-A’LANEE MENAL MUKRAMEEN.\nfor what my Lord forgave me and made me one of the honoured ones!’\nوَمَاۤ اَنْزَلْنَا عَلٰى قَوْمِهٖ مِنْۢ بَعْدِهٖ مِنْ جُنْدٍ مِّنَ السَّمَآءِ وَمَا كُنَّا مُنْزِلِيْنَ‏(28)\nWA MAA ANZALNAA A’LAA QAWMEHI MIM BA’DEHI MIN JUNDIM MENAS SAMAAA-E WA MAA KUNNAA MUNZELEEN.\nAfter him We did not send down on his people a host from the sky, nor We would have sent down.\nاِنْ كَانَتْ اِلَّا صَيْحَةً وَّاحِدَةً فَاِذَا هُمْ خٰمِدُوْنَ‏(29)\nIN KAANAT ILLAA SAY-HATANW WAAHEDATAN FA-EZAA HUM KHAAMEDOON.\nIt was but a single Cry, and, behold, they were stilled [like burnt ashes]!\nيٰحَسْرَةً عَلَى الْعِبَادِ ؔۚ مَا يَاْتِيْهِمْ مِّنْ رَّسُوْلٍ اِلَّا كَانُوْا بِهٖ يَسْتَهْزِءُوْنَ‏(30)\nYAA HASRATAN A’LAL E’BAADE, MAA YAATEEHIM MIR RASOOLIN ILLAA KAANOO BEHI YASTAHZEOON.\nHow regrettable of the servants! There did not come to them any apostle but that they used to deride him.\nاَلَمْ يَرَوْا كَمْ اَهْلَكْنَا قَبْلَهُمْ مِّنَ الْقُرُوْنِ اَنَّهُمْ اِلَيْهِمْ لَا يَرْجِعُوْنَؕ‏(31)\nALAM YARAW KAM AHLAKNAA QABLAHUM MENAL QOROONE ANNAHUM ELAYHIM LAA YARJEOON.\nHave they not regarded how many generations We have destroyed before them who will not come back to them?\nوَاِنْ كُلٌّ لَّمَّا جَمِيْعٌ لَّدَيْنَا مُحْضَرُوْنَ‏(32)\nWA IN KULLUL LAMMAA JAMEE-U’L LADAYNAA MOHZAROON.\nAnd all of them will indeed be presented before Us.\nوَاٰيَةٌ لَّهُمُ الْاَرْضُ الْمَيْتَةُ ۖۚ اَحْيَيْنٰهَا وَاَخْرَجْنَا مِنْهَا حَبًّا فَمِنْهُ يَاْكُلُوْنَ‏(33)\nWA AAYATUL LAHOMUL ARZUL MAYTAH, AHYAYNAAHAA WA AKHRAJNAA MINHAA HABBAN FAMINHO YAAKOLOON.\nA sign for them is the dead earth, which We revive and bring forth grain out of it, so they eat of it.\nوَجَعَلْنَا فِيْهَا جَنّٰتٍ مِّنْ نَّخِيْلٍ وَّاَعْنَابٍ وَّفَجَّرْنَا فِيْهَا مِنَ الْعُيُوْنِۙ‏(34)\nWA JA-A’LNAA FEEHAA JANNAATIM MIN NAKHEELINW WA A-A’NAABINW WA FAJJARNAA FEEHAA MENAL O’YOONE.\nWe make in it orchards of date palms and vines, and We cause springs to gush forth in it,\nلِيَاْكُلُوْا مِنْ ثَمَرِهٖ ۙ وَمَا عَمِلَتْهُ اَيْدِيْهِمْ ؕ اَفَلَا يَشْكُرُوْنَ‏(35)\nLE-YAAKOLOO MIN SAMAREHI, WA MAA A’MELAT-HO AYDEEHIM, AFALAA YASHKOROON.\nso that they may eat of its fruit and what their hands have cultivated. Will they not then give thanks?\nسُبْحٰنَ الَّذِىْ خَلَقَ الْاَزْوَاجَ كُلَّهَا مِمَّا تُنْۢبِتُ الْاَرْضُ وَمِنْ اَنْفُسِهِمْ وَمِمَّا لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(36)\nSUBHAANAL LAZEE KHALAQAL AZWAAJA KULLAHAA MIMMAA TUMBETUL ARZO WA MIN ANFOSEHIM WA MIMMAA LAA YA’LAMOON.\nImmaculate is He who has created all the kinds of what the earth grows, and of themselves, and of what they do not know.\nوَاٰيَةٌ لَّهُمُ الَّيْلُۖۚ نَسْلَخُ مِنْهُ النَّهَارَ فَاِذَا هُمْ مُّظْلِمُوْنَۙ‏(37)\nWA AAYATUL LAHOMUL LAYL, NASLAKHO MINHUN NAHAARA FA-EZAA HUM MUZLEMOON.\nA sign for them is the night, which We strip of daylight, and, behold, they find themselves in the dark!\nوَالشَّمْسُ تَجْرِىْ لِمُسْتَقَرٍّ لَّهَاؕ ذٰلِكَ تَقْدِيْرُ الْعَزِيْزِ الْعَلِيْمِؕ‏(38)\nWASH-SHAMSO TAJREE LE-MUSTAQARRIL LAHAA, ZAALEKA TAQDEERUL A’ZEEZIL A’LEEM.\nThe sun runs on to its place of rest: That is the ordaining of the All-mighty, the All-knowing.\nوَالْقَمَرَ قَدَّرْنٰهُ مَنَازِلَ حَتّٰى عَادَ كَالْعُرْجُوْنِ الْقَدِيْمِ‏(39)\nWAL QAMARA QADDARNAAHO MANAAZELA HATTAA A’ADA KAL-U’RJOONIL QADEEM.\nAs for the moon, We have ordained its phases, until it becomes like an old palm leaf.\nلَا الشَّمْسُ يَنْۢبَغِىْ لَهَاۤ اَنْ تُدْرِكَ الْقَمَرَ وَلَا الَّيْلُ سَابِقُ النَّهَارِؕ وَكُلٌّ فِىْ فَلَكٍ يَّسْبَحُوْنَ‏(40)\nLASH-SHAMSO YANBAGHEE LAHAA AN TUDREKAL QAMARA WA LAL LAYLO SAABEQUN NAHAARE, WA KULLUN FEE FALAKINY YASBAHOON.\nNeither it behooves the sun to overtake the moon, nor may the night outrun the day, and each swims in an orbit.\nوَاٰيَةٌ لَّهُمْ اَنَّا حَمَلْنَا ذُرِّيَّتَهُمْ فِى الْفُلْكِ الْمَشْحُوْنِۙ‏(41)\nWA AAYATUL LAHUM ANNAA HAMALNAA ZURRIYYATAHUM FIL FULKIL MASH-HOON.\nA sign for them is that We carried their progeny in the laden ship,\nوَخَلَقْنَا لَهُمْ مِّنْ مِّثْلِهٖ مَا يَرْكَبُوْنَ‏(42)\nWA KHALAQNAA LAHUM MIM MISLEHI MAA YARKABOON.\nand We have created for them what is similar to it, which they ride.\nوَاِنْ نَّشَاْ نُغْرِقْهُمْ فَلَا صَرِيْخَ لَهُمْ وَلَا هُمْ يُنْقَذُوْنَۙ‏(43)\nWA IN NASHAA NUGHRIQ-HUM FALAA SAREEKHA LAHUM WA LAA HUM YUNQAZOONA.\nAnd if We like We drown them, whereat they have no one to call for help, nor are they rescued\nاِلَّا رَحْمَةً مِّنَّا وَمَتَاعًا اِلٰى حِيْنٍ‏(44)\nILLAA RAHMATAM MINNAA WA MATAA-A’N ELAA HEEN.\nexcept by a mercy from Us and for an enjoyment until some time.\nوَاِذَا قِيْلَ لَهُمُ اتَّقُوْا مَا بَيْنَ اَيْدِيْكُمْ وَمَا خَلْفَكُمْ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُرْحَمُوْنَ‏(45)\nWA EZAA QEELA LAHOMUT TAQOO MAA BAYNA AYDEEKUM WA MAA KHALFAKUM LA-A’LLAKUM TURHA-MOON.\nAnd when they are told, ‘Beware of that which is before you and that which is behind you, so that you may receive [His] mercy…’\nوَمَا تَاْتِيْهِمْ مِّنْ اٰيَةٍ مِّنْ اٰيٰتِ رَبِّهِمْ اِلَّا كَانُوْا عَنْهَا مُعْرِضِيْنَ‏(46)\nWA MAA TAA-TEEHIM MIN AAYATIM MIN AAYAATE RABBEHIM ILLAA KAANOO A’NHAA MOA’REZEEN.\nThere does not come to them any sign from among the signs of their Lord but that they have been disregarding it.\nوَاِذَا قِيْلَ لَهُمْ اَنْفِقُوْا مِمَّا رَزَقَكُمُ اللّٰهُ ۙ قَالَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا لِلَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اَنُطْعِمُ مَنْ لَّوْ يَشَآءُ اللّٰهُ اَطْعَمَهٗٓ ۖ  اِنْ اَنْتُمْ اِلَّا فِىْ ضَلٰلٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‏(47)\nWA EZAA QEELA LAHUM ANFEQOO MIMMAA RAZAQAKOMUL LAAHO, QAALAL LAZEENA KAFAROO LILLAZEENA AAMANOO A-NUT-E’MO MAL LAW YASHAAA-UL LAAHO ATA’MAH, IN ANTUM ILLAA FEE ZALAALIM MOBEEN.\nWhen they are told, ‘Spend out of what Allah has provided you,’ the faithless say to the faithful, ‘Shall we feed [someone] whom Allah would feed, if He wished? You are only in manifest error.’\nوَيَقُوْلُوْنَ مَتٰى هٰذَا الْوَعْدُ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ صٰدِقِيْنَ‏(48)\nWA YAQOOLOONA MATAA HAAZAL WA’DO IN KUNTUM SAADEQEEN.\nAnd they say, ‘When will this promise be fulfilled, should you be truthful?’\nمَا يَنْظُرُوْنَ اِلَّا صَيْحَةً وَّاحِدَةً تَاْخُذُهُمْ وَهُمْ يَخِصِّمُوْنَ‏(49)\nMAA YANZOROONA ILLAA SAYHATANW WAAHEDATAN TAAKHOZOHUM WA HUM YAKHISSEMOON.\nThey do not await but a single Cry that will seize them as they wrangle.\nفَلَا يَسْتَطِيْعُوْنَ تَوْصِيَةً وَّلَاۤ اِلٰٓى اَهْلِهِمْ يَرْجِعُوْنَ‏(50)\nFALAA YASTATEEO’ONA TAWSEYATANW WALAA ELAA AHLEHIM YARJE-O’ON.\nThen they will not be able to make any will, nor will they return to their folks.\nوَنُفِخَ فِى الصُّوْرِ فَاِذَا هُمْ مِّنَ الْاَجْدَاثِ اِلٰى رَبِّهِمْ يَنْسِلُوْنَ‏(51)\nWA NOFEKHA FIS-SOORE FA-EZAA HUM MENAL AJDAASE ELAA RABBEHIM YANSELOON.\nAnd when the Trumpet is blown, behold, there they will be, scrambling towards their Lord from their graves!\nقَالُوْا يٰوَيْلَنَا مَنْۢ بَعَثَنَا مِنْ مَّرْقَدِنَاۘؔهٰذَا مَا وَعَدَ الرَّحْمٰنُ وَصَدَقَ الْمُرْسَلُوْنَ‏(52)\nQAALOO YAA WAYLANAA MAM BA-A’SANAA MIM MARQADENAA, HAAZAA MA WA-A’DAR RAHMAANO WA SADAQAL MURSALOON.\nThey will say, ‘Woe to us! Who raised us from our place of sleep?’ ‘This is what the All-beneficent had promised, and the apostles had spoken the truth!’\nاِنْ كَانَتْ اِلَّا صَيْحَةً وَّاحِدَةً فَاِذَا هُمْ جَمِيْعٌ لَّدَيْنَا مُحْضَرُوْنَ‏(53)\nIN KAANAT ILLAA SAYHATANW WAAHEDATAN FA-EZAA HUM JAMEE-U’L LADAYNAA MOHZAROON.\nIt will be but a single Cry, and, behold, they will all be presented before Us!\nفَالْيَوْمَ لَا تُظْلَمُ نَفْسٌ شَيْئًا وَّلَا تُجْزَوْنَ اِلَّا مَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(54)\nFALYAWMA LAA TUZLAMO NAFSOON SHAY-ANW WA LAA TUJ-ZAWNA ILLAA MAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\n‘Today no soul will be wronged in the least, nor will you be requited except for what you used to do.’\nاِنَّ اَصْحٰبَ الْجَنَّةِ الْيَوْمَ فِىْ شُغُلٍ فٰكِهُوْنَۚ‏(55)\nINNA ASHAABAL JANNATIL YAWMA FEE SHOGHOLIN FAAKEHOON.\nIndeed today the inhabitants of paradise rejoice in their engagements\nهُمْ وَاَزْوَاجُهُمْ فِىْ ظِلٰلٍ عَلَى الْاَرَآئِكِ مُتَّكِئُوْنَ‏(56)\nHUM WA AJWAAJOHUM FEE ZELAALIN A’LAL ARAAA-EKE MUTTAKEOON.\n—they and their mates, reclining on couches in the shades.\nلَهُمْ فِيْهَا فَاكِهَةٌ وَّلَهُمْ مَّا يَدَّعُوْنَ ۖۚ‏(57)\nLAHUM FEEHAA FAAKEHATUNW WA LAHUM MAA YADDAO’ON.\nThere they have fruits, and they have whatever they want.\nسَلٰمٌ قَوْلًا مِّنْ رَّبٍّ رَّحِيْمٍ‏(58)\nSALAAMUN, QAWLAM MIR-RABBIR RAHEEM.\n‘Peace!’—a watchword from the all-merciful Lord.\nوَامْتَازُوا الْيَوْمَ اَيُّهَا الْمُجْرِمُوْنَ‏(59)\nWAM TAAZUL YAWMA AYYOHAL MUJREMOON.\nAnd ‘Get apart today, you guilty ones!’\nاَلَمْ اَعْهَدْ اِلَيْكُمْ يٰبَنِىْۤ اٰدَمَ اَنْ لَّا تَعْبُدُوا الشَّيْطٰنَۚ اِنَّهٗ لَكُمْ عَدُوٌّ مُّبِيْنٌ ۙ‏(60)\nALAM A-A’HAD ELAYKUM YAA BANEE AADAMA AL-LAA TA’BODUSH-SHAYTAANA, INNAHU LAKUM A’DUWWUM MOBEEN.\n‘Did I not exhort you, O children of Adam, saying, “Do not worship Satan. He is indeed your manifest enemy.\nوَّاَنِ اعْبُدُوْنِىْؔؕ هٰذَا صِرَاطٌ مُّسْتَقِيْمٌ‏(61)\nWA ANE’-BODOONEE, HAAZAA SERAATUM MUSTAQEEM.\nWorship Me. That is a straight path”?\nوَلَقَدْ اَضَلَّ مِنْكُمْ جِبِلًّا كَثِيْرًا ؕ اَفَلَمْ تَكُوْنُوْا تَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(62)\nWA LAQAD AZALLA MINKUM JEBILLAN KASEERAA, A-FALAM TAKOONOO TA’QELOON.\nCertainly, he has led astray many of your generations. Have you not exercised your reason?\nهٰذِهٖ جَهَنَّمُ الَّتِىْ كُنْتُمْ تُوْعَدُوْنَ‏(63)\nHAAZEHI JAHANNAMUL LATEE KUNTUM TOO-A’DOON.\nThis is the hell you had been promised!\nاِصْلَوْهَا الْيَوْمَ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَكْفُرُوْنَ‏(64)\nISLAWHAL YAWMA BEMAA KUNTUM TAKFOROON.\nEnter it today, because of what you used to deny.\nاَلْيَوْمَ نَخْتِمُ عَلٰٓى اَفْوَاهِهِمْ وَتُكَلِّمُنَاۤ اَيْدِيْهِمْ وَتَشْهَدُ اَرْجُلُهُمْ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَكْسِبُوْنَ‏(65)\nAL-YAWMA NAKHTEMO A’LAA AFWAA-HEHIM WA TOKALLEMONAA AYDEEHIM WA TASH-HADO ARJOLOHUM BEMAA KAANOO YAKSEBOON.\nToday We shall seal their mouths, and their hands shall speak to Us, and their feet shall bear witness concerning what they used to earn.’\nوَلَوْ نَشَآءُ لَطَمَسْنَا عَلٰٓى اَعْيُنِهِمْ فَاسْتَبَقُوا الصِّرَاطَ فَاَنّٰى يُبْصِرُوْنَ‏(66)\nWA LAW NA-SHAAA-O LATAMASNAA A’LAA A-A’YONEHIM FASTABAQUS-SERAATA FA-ANNAA YUBSEROON.\nHad We wished We would have blotted out their eyes: then, were they to advance towards the path, how would have they seen?\nوَلَوْ نَشَآءُ لَمَسَخْنٰهُمْ عَلٰى مَكَانَتِهِمْ فَمَا اسْتَطَاعُوْا مُضِيًّا وَّلَا يَرْجِعُوْنَ‏(67)\nWA LAW NASHAAA-O LAMASAKHNAAHUM A’LAA MAKAANATEHIM FAMAS-TA-TAA-OO’ MOZIYYANW WA LAA YARJE-O’ON.\nAnd had We wished We would have deformed them in their place; then they would neither have been able to move ahead nor to return.\nوَمَنْ نُّعَمِّرْهُ نُنَكِّسْهُ فِى الْخَلْقِؕ اَفَلَا يَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(68)\nWA MAN NO-A’MMIRHO NONAKKISHO FIL KHALQE, AFALAA YA’QELOON.\nAnd whomever We give a long life, We cause him to regress in creation. Then, will they not exercise their reason?\nوَمَا عَلَّمْنٰهُ الشِّعْرَ وَمَا يَنْۢبَغِىْ لَهٗؕ اِنْ هُوَ اِلَّا ذِكْرٌ وَّقُرْاٰنٌ مُّبِيْنٌۙ‏(69)\nWA MAA A’LLAMNAAHUSH-SHE’RA WA MAA YANBAGHEE LAHU, IN HOWA ILLAA ZIKRUNW WA QURAANUM MOBEEN.\nWe did not teach him poetry, nor does it behoove him. This is just a reminder and a manifest Quran,\nلِّيُنْذِرَ مَنْ كَانَ حَيًّا وَّيَحِقَّ الْقَوْلُ عَلَى الْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(70)\nLEYUNZERA MAN KAANA HAYYANW WA YAHIQQAL QAWLO A’LAL KAAFEREEN.\nso that anyone who is alive may be warned, and that the word may come due against the faithless.\nاَوَلَمْ يَرَوْا اَنَّا خَلَقْنَا لَهُمْ مِّمَّا عَمِلَتْ اَيْدِيْنَاۤ اَنْعَامًا فَهُمْ لَهَا مٰلِكُوْنَ‏(71)\nAWALAM YARAW ANNAA KHALAQNAA LAHUM MIMMAA A’MELAT AYDEENAA AN-A’AMAN FAHUM LAHAA MAALEKOON.\nHave they not seen that We have created for them—of what Our hands have worked—cattle, so they have become their masters?\nوَذَلَّلْنٰهَا لَهُمْ فَمِنْهَا رَكُوْبُهُمْ وَمِنْهَا يَاْكُلُوْنَ‏(72)\nWA ZALLALNAAHAA LAHUM FAMINHAA RAKOOBOHIM WA MINHAA YAAKOLOON.\nAnd We made them tractable for them; so some of them make their mounts and some of them they eat.\nوَلَهُمْ فِيْهَا مَنَافِعُ وَمَشَارِبُؕ اَفَلَا يَشْكُرُوْنَ‏(73)\nWA LAHUM FEEHAA MANAAFE-O’ WA MASHAAREB, AFALAA YASHKOROON.\nThere are other benefits for them therein, and drinks. Will they not then give thanks?\nوَاتَّخَذُوْا مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ اٰلِهَةً لَّعَلَّهُمْ يُنْصَرُوْنَؕ‏(74)\nWAT-TAKHAZOO MIN DOONIL LAAHE AALEHATAL LA-A’LLAHUM YUNSAROON.\nThey have taken gods besides Allah, [hoping] that they might be helped [by the fake deities].\nلَا يَسْتَطِيْعُوْنَ نَصْرَهُمْۙ وَهُمْ لَهُمْ جُنْدٌ مُّحْضَرُوْنَ‏(75)\nLAA YASTA-TEE-O’ONA NASRAHUM, WA HUM LAHUM JUNDUM MOHZAROON.\n[But] they cannot help them, while they [themselves] are an army mobilized for their defence.\nفَلَا يَحْزُنْكَ قَوْلُهُمْۘ اِنَّا نَعْلَمُ مَا يُسِرُّوْنَ وَمَا يُعْلِنُوْنَ‏(76)\nFALAA YAHZUNKA QAWLOHUM, INNAA NA’LAMO MAA YOSIRROONA WA MAA YO’LENOON.\nSo do not let their remarks grieve you. We indeed know whatever they hide and whatever they disclose.\nاَوَلَمْ يَرَ الْاِنْسَانُ اَنَّا خَلَقْنٰهُ مِنْ نُّطْفَةٍ فَاِذَا هُوَ خَصِيْمٌ مُّبِيْنٌ‏(77)\nAWALAM YARAL INSAANO ANNAA KHALAQNAAHO MIN NUTFATIN FA-EZAA HOWA KHASEEMUM MOBEEN.\nDoes not man see that We created him from a drop of [seminal] fluid, and, behold, he is an open contender!?\nوَضَرَبَ لَنَا مَثَلًا وَّ نَسِىَ خَلْقَهٗ ؕ قَالَ مَنْ يُّحْىِ الْعِظَامَ وَهِىَ رَمِيْمٌ‏(78)\nWA-ZARABA LANAA MASALANW WA-NASEYA KHALQAH, QAALA MANY YOHYIL E’ZAAMA WA HEYA RAMEEM.\nHe draws comparisons for Us, and forgets his own creation. He says, ‘Who shall revive the bones when they have decayed?’\nقُلْ يُحْيِيْهَا الَّذِىْۤ اَنْشَاَهَاۤ اَوَّلَ مَرَّةٍ ؕ وَهُوَ بِكُلِّ خَلْقٍ عَلِيْمُ ۙ‏(79)\nQUL YOHYEEHAL LAZEE AN-SHA-A-HAA AWWALA MARRAH, WA HOWA BEKULLE KHALQIN A’LEEMO-NIL.\nSay, ‘He will revive them who produced them the first time, and He has knowledge of all creation.\nاۨلَّذِىْ جَعَلَ لَكُمْ مِّنَ الشَّجَرِ الْاَخْضَرِ نَارًا فَاِذَاۤ اَنْتُمْ مِّنْهُ تُوْقِدُوْنَ‏(80)\nLAZEE JA-A’LA LAKUM MENASH-SHAJARIL AKH-ZARE NAARAN FA-EZAA ANTUM MINHO TOOQEDOON.\nHe, who made for you fire out of the green tree, and, behold, you light fire from it!\nاَوَلَيْسَ الَّذِىْ خَلَقَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ بِقٰدِرٍ عَلٰٓى اَنْ يَّخْلُقَ مِثْلَهُمْؔؕ بَلٰی وَهُوَ الْخَلّٰقُ الْعَلِيْمُ‏(81)\nAWA LAYSAL LAZEE KHALAQAS SAMAAWAATE WAL-ARZA BE-QAADERIN A’LAA ANY-YAKHLOQA MISLAHUM, BALAA, WA HOWAL KHALLAAQUL A’LEEM.\nIs not He who created the heavens and the earth able to create the like of them? Yes indeed! He is the All-creator, the All-knowing.\nاِنَّمَاۤ اَمْرُهٗۤ اِذَاۤ اَرَادَ شَیْئًا اَنْ يَّقُوْلَ لَهٗ كُنْ فَيَكُوْنُ‏(82)\nINNAMAA AMROHU EZAA ARAADA SHAY-AN ANY YAQOOLA LAHU KUN FAYAKOON.\nAll His command, when He wills something, is to say to it ‘Be,’ and it is.\nفَسُبْحٰنَ الَّذِىْ بِيَدِهٖ مَلَكُوْتُ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ وَّاِلَيْهِ تُرْجَعُوْنَ‏(83)\nFA SUBHAANAL LAZEE BEYADEHI MALAKOOTO KULLE SHAYINW WA ELAYHE TURJA-O’ON.\nSo immaculate is He in whose hand is the dominion of all things, and to whom you shall be brought back.",
  "merits": "This Surah is ‘Makki’ and it has 83 verses. It is written in the commentary of Majma’ul Bayan whoever recites Surah Ya Sin solely for seeking the pleasure of Allah (s.w.t.), all his sins will be forgiven and he will be given the reward equal to the reward of reciting the whole Qur’an 12 times. If this Surah is recited near a person on his deathbed, then for each letter recited, 12 angels are sent to pray for his forgiveness and they remain even when the soul is being taken by the Angel of Death. The angels also take part in his funeral rites.\nIf recited near a person who is in Sakarat-ul-Mawt (on the verge of passing away), then an angel brings a drink for the dying person from Jannah and as he drinks of it, he feels greatly eased. In another narration, this Surah has been described as the key to all good in this life and in the hereafter and a safety from all evil in this life and in the hereafter. Needs are fulfilled if asked after the recitation of this Surah and the reward for its recitation is also compared to performing twenty hajj pilgrimages.\nDrinking the water in which this Surah has been dissolved cures one of a thousand types of illnesses. The Holy Prophet (S) said that everything has its heart and the heart of the Holy Qur’an is Surah Ya Sin. He (s.a.w.a.) also said that if this Surah is recited in a graveyard then all punishment is lifted, for that day, from all the graves and the reciter gets the reward equal to the sum of all the good actions performed by all those who are buried in that graveyard.\nIt is narrated from Imam Ja’far as-Sadiq (a.s.) that whoever recited this Surah in the morning will be protected from all calamities and problems during the day and whoever recites it at night will be protected from Shaitan by seventy thousand angels. Recitation of this Surah saves one from the squeezing of the grave and its other torments. Passing the difficult stages in the hereafter will also be made easy for him.\nThe sixth Imam (a.s.) also said that drinking this Surah after writing it in a mixture of rose water and saffron for seven days (it has to be written once for each day) makes a person have such a good memory that he will never forget what he hears. He will win debates and will gain great respect and status. If given to a woman, her breast-milk will increase.\nKeeping this Surah in one’s possession as a talisman acts as a protection from the jealousy of people. The wearer remains safe from the evil designs of men and Jinn. It also acts as a cure from disease."
